                "Welcome to the Industrial Significant Risk Transfer (SRT) War Room Simulator. In this executive laboratory, you are appointed Head of Capital Structuring and Credit Portfolio Management at a Tier 1 global commercial bank. Your institution faces a critical strategic challenge: the bank's Common Equity Tier 1 (CET1) ratio has drifted to 11.80%, uncomfortably close to the board's mandatory risk-appetite floor of 11.50%. Issuing €1.0 billion of new common equity shares in public equity markets would trigger severe dilution and depress the bank's stock price. The CEO and Board of Directors have mandated your desk to structure an institutional synthetic Significant Risk Transfer transaction on a €12.0 billion portfolio of high-grade performing European corporate loans to release at least €800 million of locked-up regulatory capital while preserving client confidentiality and relationship franchises.",
